---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { tiers } from '../lib/offer';
import { company, supportEmail } from '../lib/site';
---

<Legal
  title="Terms"
  description="The terms for the hosted OpenMinutes service. The software itself is licensed under the AGPL-3.0."
  updated="24 October 2026"
>
  <h2>The software and the service</h2>
  <p>
    OpenMinutes is open source under the <a href="https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html">AGPL-3.0</a>
    and free to run yourself. The licence file in the repository governs the software; nothing here
    restricts the rights it gives you. These terms cover only the hosted service and this website,
    where <a href={company.url} rel="noopener">{company.name}</a>, {company.address} (KvK {company.kvk}, VAT {company.btw}), runs an instance for you.
    By ordering the hosted service you accept these terms. If you order for a company, you confirm
    you may bind it.
  </p>

  <h2>What the service is</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A running instance of OpenMinutes, with HTTPS, updates, security patches and backups.</li>
    <li>
      The setup is yours. You create the Google and Microsoft apps, enter your own provider keys,
      connect your own calendars and set up email, as on a self-hosted install.
    </li>
    <li>
      No AI usage is included. You pay your own providers directly. Whisper can run locally on the
      instance.
    </li>
    <li>
      A plan sets how many meetings the bot can sit in at the same moment: {
        tiers.map((t) => `${t.concurrent} for EUR ${t.monthly}`).join(', ')
      } a month. More on request.
    </li>
    <li>Support is by email at <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ordering and start</h2>
  <p>
    You ask for an instance with the form on the <a href="/hosting">hosting page</a>. A request is
    not a contract. The contract starts when we confirm by email that your instance is ready. We may
    decline a request.
  </p>

  <h2>Price and payment</h2>
  <p>
    Monthly, excluding VAT, with unlimited users, meetings and meeting hours on every plan. We
    invoice by email and you pay within 14 days of the invoice date. If you do not pay on time we
    may suspend the instance after a reminder, and your data is kept as described in the
    <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> while it is suspended. We may change prices with at
    least 30 days' notice by email; you can cancel before the change takes effect.
  </p>

  <h2>Cancelling</h2>
  <p>
    You can cancel at any time by email, with no minimum term, and the service runs until the end
    of the paid month. We do not refund a month that has started. Export your data before the end:
    afterwards it is deleted as described in the privacy page. We may end the service with 30 days'
    notice, or at once if you break these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Record only where you are allowed to, tell participants, and follow the laws and policies
      that apply to you. See the <a href="/docs/consent-and-legal">consent notes</a>. You are
      responsible for the content you record and process.
    </li>
    <li>Keep your keys and logins safe, and do not use the service for anything unlawful.</li>
    <li>
      Do not attack, overload or try to get around the limits of the service, and do not resell it
      without our agreement.
    </li>
    <li>
      Automating a Google account can go against Google's terms. The risk of using a Meet bot
      account is yours. The same goes for the terms of your AI and calendar providers.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    You own your recordings, transcripts and minutes, and we claim no rights in them beyond running
    the service for you. You can export them and move to self-hosting at any time. See the
    <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a> for how we process them, including our role as your
    processor.
  </p>

  <h2>Availability and support</h2>
  <p>
    This is a small operation. We aim to keep the service running and to answer by email, but we do
    not guarantee a response time or uptime. Instances are set up by hand, up to 1 business day at
    launch. We may do maintenance that interrupts the service, and we try to announce long
    interruptions in advance. Backups are made to help us restore the service; you should also export
    minutes you cannot lose.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    The service is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for indirect
    loss such as lost profit, lost meetings or missed recordings, or for what your providers or
    Google and Microsoft do, and our total liability is limited to the fees you paid in the three
    months before the claim. Nothing here limits liability for intent or deliberate recklessness, or
    liability that cannot be limited by law.
  </p>

  <h2>Consumers</h2>
  <p>
    The hosted service is meant for businesses and professionals. If you are a consumer, the
    mandatory consumer protection rules of your country still apply and prevail over these terms.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    The website and docs are provided as they are. The OpenMinutes name and logo are not covered by
    the AGPL; please do not use them in a way that suggests we endorse a modified version or a
    service we do not run.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes and law</h2>
  <p>
    We will tell you by email before these terms change in a way that matters, and the change applies
    from your next paid month. Dutch law applies. Disputes go to the competent court in the
    Netherlands, unless mandatory law gives you another court. Questions:
    <a href={`mailto:${supportEmail}`}>{supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</Legal>
